    "/api/v1/creators/compare": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Return bounded personal side-by-side comparison for the requested creator keys.\n\nCompares 2-4 canonical creators using the same explainable personal analytics\nalready available on creator detail pages. Every metric remains explicitly\npersonal to the authenticated user.\n\nMetrics included per creator:\n- Average rating and median rating\n- Rated sample count\n- Rating distribution\n- 5★/top-rating rate (proportion of 5.0 ratings)\n- Role-specific averages and counts\n- Strongest series/thread aggregates\n- Unread attributed issue count (Issue.status == \"unread\", not queue/upcoming semantics)\n- Read-but-unrated attributed issue count (no stored effective rating)\n- Explicit \"insufficient data\" flag when rated sample < 3\n\nOnly creator keys visible in the authenticated user's own confirmed issue\nmetadata are compared; unknown or foreign keys are silently omitted so a\ncreator key can never leak another user's library state. Same-display-name\ncreators remain distinct via their canonical keys.\n\nArgs:\n    current_user: Authenticated user whose library is aggregated.\n    keys: Comma-separated canonical creator keys (2-4).\n    db: Async database session.\n\nReturns:\n    Batch comparison keyed by requested visible creator keys, plus explicit\n    coverage state and list of keys with insufficient data.\n\nRaises:\n    HTTPException: When the ``keys`` parameter is missing, out of bounds, or malformed.",
        "operationId": "compare_creators_endpoint_api_v1_creators_compare_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Comma-separated canonical creator keys (2-4)",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "keys",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "Comma-separated canonical creator keys (2-4)",
              "title": "Keys"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreatorComparisonResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Compare Creators Endpoint",
        "tags": [
          "creators",
          "creators"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/creators/discoveries": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Return explainable personal taste-discovery views for the authenticated user.\n\nEvery view is deterministic and derived only from the user's own latest\neffective ratings and confirmed creator credits. A creator may appear in\nmultiple views, and each entry carries the supporting metrics and the exact\nrules that qualified it, so no ranking is unexplained. Every view has an\nexplicit minimum sample before it ranks creators, and missing creator\nmetadata is reported as partial coverage rather than negative evidence.\n\nArgs:\n    current_user: Authenticated user whose library is aggregated.\n    db: Async database session.\n\nReturns:\n    Bounded discovery views in canonical order plus metadata-coverage state.",
        "operationId": "get_creator_discoveries_endpoint_api_v1_creators_discoveries_get",
